Author: Kenneth Jiang <kenneth.jiang@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 11:26:52 2026 -0700

    Let a header button take the surface it sits on

    A Quiet or Outline HeaderButton filled itself with surface-canvas at rest,
    the project header's surface. On a dialog header, which is surface-raised,
    the two tokens differ in dark mode and the button drew a lighter box
    behind its icon. HeaderButton::set_surface(HeaderSurface::Raised) makes
    the button take the raised surface instead. The default stays Canvas, so
    every existing button draws as before.

